<title>INDIA: INDIAN SOYBEAN UP, OIL STRONG, MEAL STEADY.</title>
<headline>INDIAN SOYBEAN UP, OIL STRONG, MEAL STEADY.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were slightly up in central Indian markets today. Business volume was dull and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained strong on good demand in local markets. Prices were up by 100 rupees per tonne today. Business volume was good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in very thin trading. Soymeal yellow was $265-266 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) at west Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $96-97 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,250-3,300 per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
